      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear the devastation in your words and understand why reassurances about your worth feel hollow when you have truly outlived the systems that defined you; consequently, grief over lost purpose is not a personal failing but a rational response to profound loss. While it is painful to admit when something ends, forcing yourself to continue walking a path that no longer exists often feels more like a punishment than hope. You are not alone in this erosion of self, and reaching out to a specialized therapist who understands clinician burnout might offer you a space where listening without offering clichés is actually what you need right now.",
